        "original_id": "dc2b88b0-a992-55c5-be93-e822f435dd5f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Now Show\n- Organizations: BBC Radio 4\n- People: Jon Holmes, Laura Shavin, Emma Kennedy, Sue Perkins, Marcus Brigstocke, Mitch Benn, Pippa Evans, Adam Kay, Susan Elizabeth Sue Perkins\n- Roles: comedian, broadcaster, actress, writer\n- Places: East Dulwich, south London\n- Topics: radio comedy, satire, weekly news\n\nFacts:\n- The Now Show is a British radio comedy broadcast on BBC Radio 4 that satirises the week's news.\n- The Now Show features skits from Jon Holmes and Laura Shavin.\n- Earlier series of The Now Show featured Emma Kennedy, and sometimes Sue Perkins, for the female voices.\n- The Now Show includes a monologue by Marcus Brigstocke.\n- The Now Show includes music by Mitch Benn, Pippa Evans, or Adam Kay.\n- Susan Elizabeth \"Sue\" Perkins was born on 22 September 1969.\n- Sue Perkins is an English comedian, broadcaster, actress, and writer.\n- Sue Perkins was born in East Dulwich in south London.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
